{"agent":"bg110","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The added branch still treats any ancestor of HEAD as a valid `--reviewed-sha` once the branch has no commits of its own. `merge-base --is-ancestor full head` is true for every commit in base history when head is at base, and nothing checks that `full` is that item's merged commit. The new test demonstrates it: T1 is claimed onto a branch at base and `--reviewed-sha` is `m1`, an older commit that was never T1's landing; standards records passed and stores that sha. A re-claim with no new work can therefore re-pass standards against unrelated history.","digest":"bc77dab8dfab9e14","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/gates/_vet.py:222","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/gates/_vet.py:222"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The stated bug is also that `gate record implement --outcome passed` refuses with \"no commit ahead of main\" after a re-claim that cleared `merged_sha` and left a branch with zero commits ahead. This hunk only returns success from the standards reviewed-sha check. The same re-claim input still cannot re-pass implement, and nothing here restores or consults the prior landing for that gate. The regression test only covers standards.","digest":"af85ed753b6d0057","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/gates/_vet.py:222","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/gates/_vet.py:222"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":2762,"diff_sha":"60345d72e6bc1edd855ba60fe71f46a88a9ca3e4eb3d241c206ebc5cd08285d1","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B600455cc2a","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":10.3,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"8ed454a55e43f7e8","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B600455cc2a.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261109T031328Z-b074